    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class is the only test class; the other two files are the base and a helper) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is rejected with HTTP 400, following the codebase's existing validator \u2192 exception \u2192 advice pattern:\n\n1. **`RegistrationDateValidator`** (new `@Component`) \u2014 single responsibility: rejects a supplied date that `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`. A `null` date is left untouched (the controller still defaults it to today), so only explicitly-supplied future dates are rejected.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `CityCapacityExceededException`/`DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` exceptions.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected the validator (constructor + field, matching the existing collaborators) and call `registrationDateValidator.validate(owner.getRegistrationDate())` before the date is defaulted/business-day-adjusted.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler` for `FutureRegistrationDateException` returning `400 Bad Request` via the shared `detailBuild` helper, consistent with the other domain exception handlers.\n\nThe new logic stays isolated in its own small validator rather than being inlined into the controller, reusing the established error-response machinery.",
